# Durations of more units than machine integers hold

The components of a duration are machine integers: multiplying a duration by
an integer beyond them is a runtime error, not a wrapped or truncated result.

```catala
declaration scope Overflow:
  input n content integer
  output d content duration

scope Overflow:
  definition d equals 2 day * n
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Overflow --input {"n":"4611686018427387903"}
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: an integer is too large for this computation.
│
├─➤ tests/date/bad/duration_overflow.catala_en:12.29-30:
│    │
│ 12 │   definition d equals 2 day * n
│    │                             ‾
└─ Durations of more units than machine integers hold
#return code 123#
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Overflow --input {"n":"-100000000000000000000000000000"}
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: an integer is too large for this computation.
│
├─➤ tests/date/bad/duration_overflow.catala_en:12.29-30:
│    │
│ 12 │   definition d equals 2 day * n
│    │                             ‾
└─ Durations of more units than machine integers hold
#return code 123#
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Overflow --input {"n":"1000"} -F json
{"d":{"years":0,"months":0,"days":2000}}
```
